    "result_text": "The full test suite passes with **BUILD SUCCESS** (Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `Owner` model already had `customerCode` and `registrationDate` fields; the only missing piece was the audit emission. In `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, after a successful `saveOwner`, I added an audit line via a logger named `AUDIT`:\n\n- Added SLF4J imports and a `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");`\n- After the owner is persisted (so `owner.getId()` is populated), emit:\n  ```java\n  AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nPlacing it after `saveOwner` ensures the id is assigned and that the line is only emitted on a genuinely successful create (all validation/quota/conflict rejections return earlier). The test asserts an `AUDIT` log line containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` \u2014 all three are present, and the observed line confirms it (`AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07`).",
